traceability.evidence:
Traceability annotations in implementation:
- src/index.ts header:
  /**
   * ESLint Traceability Plugin
   * @story docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md
   * @req REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE - Provide foundational plugin export and registration
   * @req REQ-ERROR-HANDLING - Gracefully handles plugin loading errors and missing dependencies
   */,Core plugin structure, rule registry, configs, and error handling (src/index.ts):
- RULE_NAMES constant enumerates all rule files:
  const RULE_NAMES = [
    "require-story-annotation",
    "require-req-annotation",
    "require-branch-annotation",
    "valid-annotation-format",
    "valid-story-reference",
    "valid-req-reference",
    "prefer-implements-annotation",
    "require-test-traceability",
  ] as const;

- Dynamic rule registry and ES module compatibility:
  const rules: Record = {} as any;
  RULE_NAMES.forEach((name) => {
    try {
      const mod = require(`./rules/${name}`);
      rules[name] = mod.default ?? mod;
    } catch (error: any) {
      console.error(
        `[eslint-plugin-traceability] Failed to load rule "${name}": ${error.message}`,
      );
      rules[name] = {
        meta: {
          type: "problem",
          docs: {
            description: `Failed to load rule '${name}'`,
          },
          schema: [],
        },
        create(context: Rule.RuleContext) {
          return {
            Program(node: any) {
              context.report({
                node,
                message: `eslint-plugin-traceability: Error loading rule "${name}": ${error.message}`,
              });
            },
          };
        },
      } as Rule.RuleModule;
    }
  });

- Flat-config presets & config system:
  const TRACEABILITY_RULE_SEVERITIES = {
    "traceability/require-story-annotation": "error",
    "traceability/require-req-annotation": "error",
    "traceability/require-branch-annotation": "error",
    "traceability/valid-annotation-format": "warn",
    "traceability/valid-story-reference": "error",
    "traceability/valid-req-reference": "error",
    "traceability/require-test-traceability": "error",
  } as const;

  function createTraceabilityFlatConfig() {
    return {
      rules: {
        ...TRACEABILITY_RULE_SEVERITIES,
      },
    };
  }

  const configs = {
    recommended: [createTraceabilityFlatConfig()],
    strict: [createTraceabilityFlatConfig()],
  };

  const plugin = { rules, configs?, maintenance? };
  plugin.configs = configs;
  plugin.maintenance = { detectStaleAnnotations, updateAnnotationReferences, batchUpdateAnnotations, verifyAnnotations, generateMaintenanceReport };

  export { rules, configs, maintenance };
  export default plugin;,ESLint v9 flat-config integration for development and tests (eslint.config.js):
- Uses ESLint v9 flat config format (array of config objects).
- Dynamically loads the plugin from ./src/index.js or ./lib/src/index.js, with CI-aware error handling:
  try { plugin = require("./src/index.js"); } catch (eSrc) {
    try { plugin = require("./lib/src/index.js"); } catch (eLib) {
      const inCI = process.env.NODE_ENV === "ci" || process.env.CI === "true";
      if (inCI) {
        throw new Error("Traceability plugin not found. Expected ./src/index.js or ./lib/src/index.js to be present in CI.");
      } else {
        console.warn("Traceability plugin not built yet, skipping traceability rules");
        plugin = {};
      }
    }
  }
- Integrates plugin into flat config via plugins: { ...(plugin.rules ? { traceability: plugin } : {}) } in JS and TS file configs.,NPM package structure and TypeScript usage (package.json):
